{#
calendar/_invite_response.stream.html.twig
─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
The answer to an RSVP: the card as it now reads, and a toast for the half the
card cannot show.

The card shows the status that was recorded, which happens whether or not the
organiser could be reached. Whether they WERE reached is the toast — a reply
that never left is the case worth interrupting somebody about, because an
organiser who did not hear "no" is still holding a seat.

Variables:
  invite        MessageInvite|null  null only if the invitation vanished mid-request
  toastMessage  string              translation key
  toastType     string              success | error
#}
{% if invite is not null %}
    <turbo-stream action="replace" target="invite_card_{{ invite.message.id }}">
        <template>
            {% include 'calendar/_invite_card.html.twig' with { invite: invite } only %}
        </template>
    </turbo-stream>
{% endif %}

<turbo-stream action="append" target="toast-region">
    <template>
        {% include '_partials/_toast.html.twig' with {
            message: toastMessage|trans,
            type: toastType,
        } %}
    </template>
</turbo-stream>
